  "notes": [
    "The batcher's key is RFC 8032 §7.1's published specification test key, not a real one. Its private half is public, so every promise here is reproducible, and no real batcher key exists anywhere in this repository: the engine has no place to keep one.",
    "The master key is a specification test key, not a real one: its bytes spell out what it is. Every epoch key, slot and padding leaf here follows from it, so the whole tree is reproducible. A real k_master never appears in this repository (INV-TREE-05).",
    "§1.6 signs the SPI digest, not its preimage. Both are recorded so an implementation that disagrees can tell which half it built wrongly.",
    "A root published after the window confirms the breach rather than rebutting it, which is why the same proof is accepted at one epoch and refused at the next (D-72)."
  ],
